    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d184">

                <pb facs="0311" n="229" xml:id="pg229"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">867n.01/446: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Great Britain</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Houghton</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                    State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >London</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1925-11-24T10:00:00+00:00"><hi rendition="#italic">November 24,
                                1925—10 a.m.</hi></date><lb/>[Received November 24—7:09
                        a.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>356. Department’s 344, November 23, 3 p.m.<anchor n="42" xml:id="d184-f1"/>
                    Informally advised by Foreign Office that I may expect reply to Embassy’s note
                    based on Department’s instruction number 224, October 13th, to be somewhat
                    further delayed due to inundation of work on Treaty Department caused by recent
                    royal death.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Houghton</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
